      "node_id": "kg_doc_1",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "François Coli (June 5, 1881 – presumably on or after May 8, 1927) was a French pilot and navigator best known as the one-eyed flying partner of Charles Nungesser in their doomed attempt to fly the Atlantic Ocean on the aircraft known as \"L'Oiseau Blanc\".",
