    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_4",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Charles Eugène Jules Marie Nungesser, MC (15 March 1892 – presumably on or after 8 May 1927) was a French ace pilot and adventurer, best remembered as a rival of Charles Lindbergh. Nungesser was a renowned ace in France, ranking third highest in the country with 43 air combat victories during World War I.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999929161806,
      "temperature": 0.9999999929161806,
